```jinja
{{ 'test1' | hash('sha1') }}
{{ 'test1' | hash('md5') }}
{{ 'test2' | checksum }}
{{ 'passwordsaresecret' | password_hash('sha512') }}            # random salt
{{ 'secretpassword' | password_hash('sha256', 'mysecretsalt') }}
```

Idempotent per host:

```jinja
{{ 'secretpassword' | password_hash('sha512', 65534 | random(seed=inventory_hostname) | string) }}
```

`rounds=` is supported for some types (2.7+). `hash` uses hashlib; `password_hash` uses **passlib** (falls back to `crypt`), so output differs depending on whether passlib is installed.
